reims-vgpu: census of where `sampled_phase resolve_us` goes, by rung.

`resolve_us` is the largest column of a Home-swipe drain second (247-308
ms/s against ~400 sampled draws on a running device) and is one scope around
the sampled ladder. Route counters say which rung served
(`gvaw_no_entry`, `zc_lin_no_alias`, `lin_memo_hit`, `buftex_*`); nothing
said what each rung cost or how many guest bytes it moved.
Now: `runtime::resolve_split` spans (nested in ResolveSource, not a
partition) charge time, count and bytes to the GVA-resident probe, the
zero-copy probe, the memo's writeback settle, its whole-span guest re-read,
its compare, its convert-on-miss, and the buffer-texture row read; one
`sampled_resolve_split` line per census second after `sampled_phase`.
Measurement only: no route, no byte and no ordering changes.
Test: runtime::resolve_split::tests.

